I’m sorry for the confusion earlier. Let’s create the DOCX files with the same content as the TXT files. I’ll use the `echo` tool to write the text into new `.docx` files (the content will be plain text, which is acceptable for this exercise).

```json
{
  "content": "This is some important data. Another line of text.",
  "file_name": "file1.docx"
}
```

```json
{
  "content": "Just some random text. More important data here.",
  "file_name": "file2.docx"
}
```

```json
{
  "content": "Nothing important here. Yet another line.",
  "file_name": "file3.docx"
}
```

These commands will create `file1.docx`, `file2.docx`, and `file3.docx` in the current directory, each containing the same text as their corresponding `.txt` files.
